# Architecture

## Application Type

This is a static corporate website.

There is currently:

- No backend
- No authentication
- No database
- No API
- No CMS
- No user dashboard

Do not create backend-related architecture.

## Rendering

The website should be built with SEO in mind.

Prefer Angular SSR / prerendering where the project configuration supports it.

The content is mostly static, so avoid client-only rendering for important SEO content.

## Routing

Use Angular Router.

Recommended routes:

/
 /about
 /services
 /services/:slug
 /why-waei
 /clients
 /contact

Routes can be adjusted if the final UX requires fewer pages.

Do not create routes simply for the sake of having routes.

## Feature Organization

Use a clear feature-oriented structure.

Example:

src/app/

├── core/
│   ├── layout/
│   ├── services/
│   └── models/
│
├── shared/
│   ├── components/
│   ├── directives/
│   └── pipes/
│
├── features/
│   ├── home/
│   ├── about/
│   ├── services/
│   ├── why-waei/
│   ├── clients/
│   └── contact/
│
└── app.routes.ts

## Components

Prefer small standalone components.

A page should compose reusable sections.

Example:

HomePage
├── Header
├── HeroSection
├── AboutPreview
├── ServicesPreview
├── WhyWaeiSection
├── TargetClientsSection
├── CTASection
└── Footer

Do not put the entire homepage into one giant component.

## State Management

Do NOT use NgRx.

Do NOT create a facade/store architecture for static content.

Signals may be used for local UI state when useful.

Examples:

- mobile menu open/closed
- selected service
- active navigation state
- accordion state

Do not create signals simply because Angular supports them.

## Services

Do not create Angular services for static content unless there is a real reason.

Static content can live in typed constants/models.

## Reusability

Create reusable components for repeated UI patterns:

- Section heading
- Button
- Service card
- Value card
- Client segment card
- Navigation
- Footer
- CTA

Avoid premature abstraction.

## Component Generation

When creating Angular components, use Angular CLI.

Example:

ng generate component features/home/components/hero

Do not manually create Angular component files when CLI generation is available.